## Commands
Run from `/home/udai/common/compass`, on branch `fix/epf-opening-section-dedup`.
Report the literal output and exit code of every command.

1. `git status --porcelain` (before)
2. `git add` each of the 14 paths above, explicitly listed
3. `git diff --cached --name-only` — must be exactly those 14
4. `git status --porcelain` — confirm `screen-shots/` is still untracked (`??`)
5. Commit with this message, via a heredoc so the trailer is preserved:

```
fix(web): remove duplicate EpfOpeningSection and read opening balance from the ledger

PR #191 was squash-merged onto a main that already carried an EpfOpeningSection
from #189, which this branch (forked at caa5f2d) never contained. The squash
replayed our diff on top of it, leaving two top-level declarations of the same
function and failing the build with TS2393 at AccountDetailPage.tsx:308 and :439.
main has not compiled since, and v2.8.13 published no images.

Delete the redundant single-field EpfOpeningSection added by #191 and keep #189's
EPS-aware component, which owns the "Of which, EPS" split.

Repoint that surviving component's total field from account.openingBalancePaise
to account.openingTransactionPaise at all four read sites (state initialiser,
effect body, effect dependency array, dirty comparison). The column is pinned at
0 for every account type because opening balances are held as an is_opening
ledger transaction, so seeding from it blanked the field after every save and
left Save permanently enabled. The PATCH body still sends openingBalancePaise,
which is the correct write field.

Because the later of two same-named function declarations wins at runtime, the
previous fix would have been a silent no-op even if it had compiled.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
```

